{
  "schema_version": "formalization-faithfulness-1",
  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-COORDINATE-DIRECTIONAL-METHODS-INTERPRETED-PRODUCTION-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "judge classifications differ",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C08 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The classification is not-faithful-weaker. Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, the target preserves conservative sequential execution but does not characterize the constituent high-resolution directional methods. The reverse implication concerns the complete conditional proposition, not an assertion that every source method supplies its premises.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 6, Section 1.3 describes extending one-dimensional high-resolution methods by successive coordinate problems. The elaborated target universally quantifies rule, admitted, reference, oldError, and faceError and places their qualifications before the conclusion. D006–D009 and D037–D039 define conservative updates and ordered composition without a high-resolution qualification."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The requested object-linkage and applicability review confirms limitations without making the conditional identities indeterminate. Q10 permits supplied geometry and coordinate connectivity. It does not supply omitted constituent-method semantics or identify arbitrary physical regions and fluxes with the independently quantified Cartesian objects.",
      "primary_evidence": "Q10 selects coordinate connectivity, supplied physical volumes and shared normal face fluxes, and successive conservative coordinate-line updates. D029 supplies measured regions and closure incidence. The target's Cartesian branch assumes only equality of volume functions and equality with an area-weighted numerical rule."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "The unresolved questions do not prevent a definite weaker classification. The target's missing method characterization establishes failure of the forward implication. Its additional premises and conditional Cartesian branch are sufficiently explicit to establish the reverse implication at their actual logical scope. Neither satisfiability nor additional conditional estimates establish faithful strength.",
      "primary_evidence": "The fully explicit target exposes the complete implication structure. Its substantive conclusions are composition, conservative balances, line locality, a conditional discrepancy bound, and conditional Cartesian identities. None concludes existence of suitable stage references, general grid representability, or a high-resolution method."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "Binder meaning is resolved: D is a finite direction type, m is the independent positive state-component count, cells are the full integer coordinate lattice, and Point and FacePoint are separately supplied spaces. Nonempty stages force D to be inhabited. This is a definite representation with a domain limitation, not an unknown type interpretation.",
      "primary_evidence": "The elaborated target has [Fintype D], 0 < m, stages : List (D × Real), stages ≠ [], and cell arguments D → Int. D029 and D044 expose the physical-space structures and partition requirements. No finite boundary-cell index type or periodic quotient appears."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The hypotheses are explicit additional applicability conditions. Q10 supports the geometric abstraction, and the inherited receipt supports integral treatment of discontinuities within its stated scope. Neither establishes automatic availability of admitted prefix states or stage references. Such availability is not concluded by the target. Flux differentiability is state differentiability and does not impose spatial smoothness on q.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target assumes hreferences, hadmitted, hstates, hold, and hface for every actual prefix. D012 requires reference integrability and admissibility. D020/D032 require a Fréchet derivative of the flux on admissible states. Printed pages 4–5 distinguish solution smoothness from integral conservation at discontinuities."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C08 unclear",
      "resolution": "The physical and numerical quantities are distinct, but the Cartesian identification is limited. The branch proves product-box measures and reduction of the same algebraic executor when its volumes and rule match. It does not identify data.cells.cellRegion with those boxes, data.faceMeasure with transverse measure, or data.normalFlux with the separately quantified flux. These absent identifications cannot be inferred, but they are also not claims whose truth is needed for the conditional branch.",
      "primary_evidence": "D014–D019 define physical cell means, physical face integrals, and temporal averages independently of D008's numerical flux. The final target branch quantifies axes and lineRule with two equality premises, then independently quantifies flux and q. Its last conclusion is D010 for explicitly constructed means and fluxes, not data.ReferenceOn for that q."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The specialization and generalization are identifiable. The target permits abstract measured partitions and one-direction instances while using a full integer lattice. It establishes no representation theorem for arbitrary finite or periodic source grids. This limits claims of source coverage; it does not invalidate the stated conditional theorem or make it a stronger version of the source.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 6 states rectangular or logically rectangular geometry without prescribing an infinite lattice. D029 uses cells indexed by D → Int, with positive finite measure for every cell. D035 supplies integer-indexed adjacent positive intervals. Q10 does not assert a boundary-extension theorem."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "No stage-reference existence or well-posedness theorem is asserted. More decisively, the stage reference predicate does not certify a directional solution throughout the substep: it imposes conservation only between the selected endpoints. The inherited rectangle interpretation cannot strengthen that definition. This is a resolved failure of solution linkage, not merely an unanswered existence question.",
      "primary_evidence": "D010 at s,t contains one endpoint mass-change identity for each cell. D012 adds integrability and membership throughout the interval but no universally quantified subinterval balance. With zero physical flux and unrestricted admissible states, q(x,τ)=τ(h−τ)v for nonzero v satisfies ReferenceOn on [0,h] on finite-volume cells, yet violates conservation between 0 and h/2. D021, by contrast, explicitly quantifies all rectangle endpoints."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The reverse implication is yes for the exact conditional proposition under Q10 and the applicable inherited interpretation. It does not require deriving the theorem's premises from the source. Given those premises, unfolding the update and fold yields composition, local balance, telescoping, and locality; subtracting the assumed physical endpoint balance yields the error estimate. Product measures, positive widths, and the separately assumed rectangle law yield the Cartesian branch.",
      "primary_evidence": "D006–D009, D037, D039, and D209 specify the executor. D010, D019, and D038 give the endpoint balance and temporal normalization. D001–D005 and D035 give Cartesian factors and adjacency. D021 supplies all rectangle identities conditionally. The native supplement identifies Real.measureSpace with the usual normalized real measure through Real.volume_eq_stieltjes_id and Real.volume_Ioc."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity, conditional consistency, and purported strength",
      "resolution": "The target has satisfiable, nonconstant executions and is not globally vacuous. However, admission of actual lines does not imply admission of constants, and unrestricted error bounds impose no smallness or refinement requirement. These semantic weaknesses survive the supplied nonvacuity evidence. Additional assumptions and auxiliary estimates therefore do not justify faithful-stronger.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplied native PhysicalIntervalSweep.simultaneous_contract and nonconstant_execution declarations exhibit simultaneous physical/reference/execution content and changed cell values. The separate two-direction executor witness does not assert the full physical contract in two dimensions. In the target, hconstant is guarded by admitted on constant lines; hold and hface allow bounds equal to their respective discrepancy norms."
    },
    {
      "item": "Disputed dependency meanings, signs, norms, and interpretation scope",
      "resolution": "The disputed local definitions have determinate meanings. D025 is a flux-difference formula despite its Riemann-related name; imported solver structures do not qualify the arbitrary target rule. The conservative signs and offsets are correct. The auxiliary norm is the finite maximum norm, and the inequality is conditional error propagation rather than a stability or convergence assertion. The inherited receipt does not authorize global extensions or unspecified face representatives.",
      "primary_evidence": "D025 subtracts dt/width times edgeFlux(i+1)−edgeFlux(i). D007/D037 use the corresponding outward-flux sign, agreeing with equation (1.10) on printed page 4. D108 gives the supremum of component norms. The inherited receipt expressly limits its scope to the Chapter 1 discontinuity discussion and preserves source ambiguity."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "Even under the recorded coordinator-selected Q10 interpretation and the applicable inherited discontinuity convention, the target establishes a conditional conservative executor rather than the source's extension of one-dimensional high-resolution methods. Coordinate locality, shared fluxes, and chronological coverage are genuine, but no hypothesis identifies the arbitrary rule as such a constituent method. Constant consistency may be gated away, and discrepancy bounds may be arbitrarily large. Even with all constants admitted, on unit Cartesian cells with scalar identity physical flux, a rule F_i=U_{i−1}+K(U_i−U_{i−1}) is constant-consistent and conservative for arbitrary K; zero reference fields and exact discrepancy norms satisfy the reference and error premises without establishing a high-resolution method. Additionally, ReferenceOn requires only the selected endpoint balance and admits fields that violate conservation inside the substep. Q10 specifies geometry and conservative execution; it does not erase these source roles."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected Q10 interpretation, the exact Lean proposition is a conditional consequence of its explicitly supplied data and hypotheses using ordinary algebra and integration. Ordered folding yields prefix/suffix composition; the flux-difference update yields weighted cell balance, finite-line telescoping, and line locality. Subtracting D010's assumed endpoint reference balance and applying the triangle inequality yields the displayed maximum-norm bound. Positive Cartesian widths and transverse products yield measured boxes and the one-dimensional executor identity. The final rectangle-law premise yields the area-scaled directional balance, with the inherited interpretation used only within its applicable conservation scope. This does not assert that the printed source supplies every reference, admission certificate, boundary extension, or Cartesian realization. Their absence from the source limits applicability and the forward implication, rather than refuting this weaker conditional proposition."
    }
  },
  "classification": "not-faithful-weaker",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The printed source leaves logical rectangularity, coordinate-to-normal relations, substep scheduling details, and discontinuity trace/regularity conventions underspecified. Q10 and the inherited receipt remain separate, scoped interpretations rather than printed assertions.",
    "The supplied evidence does not establish representation of arbitrary finite or periodic grids by the full integer-lattice physical-data model, or availability of its reference and admission premises for every intended source method. No such general coverage is claimed here.",
    "I inspected the attached primary-source renderings and inline declaration evidence without tools. Source, rendering, transport, and runtime hashes were supplied provenance and were not independently recomputed."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "missing-constituent-method-semantics",
      "evidence": "Printed page 6, Section 1.3 starts from one-dimensional high-resolution methods. D008 accepts an arbitrary coordinate-line rule; hconstant is admission-conditional, and hold/hface have unrestricted real bounds.",
      "impact": "The target can describe conservative executions without establishing that they extend the source's constituent numerical methods. This prevents the forward implication under Q10."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "endpoint-balance-is-not-solutionhood",
      "evidence": "D010 checks one selected time interval, and D012 adds no conservation requirement for its subintervals. For zero flux, the spatially constant reference τ(h−τ)v has equal endpoint means on [0,h] but unequal means on [0,h/2].",
      "impact": "A supplied reference satisfying the target need not solve the directional conservation problem during the stage. The all-rectangle predicate in the separate Cartesian implication does not repair this."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "limited-cartesian-identification",
      "evidence": "The Cartesian branch matches only data.cellVolume and the area-weighted numerical rule; its physical flux and one-dimensional field are separately quantified.",
      "impact": "It supplies a measured algebraic specialization of the executor, not an identification of all actual physical geometry and flux objects with a Cartesian problem."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "nonvacuity-does-not-establish-faithfulness",
      "evidence": "The native simultaneous-contract and nonconstant-execution declarations support satisfiability. They do not impose approximation quality on every universally quantified rule.",
      "impact": "Global vacuity is not the reason for rejection. Nontrivial examples cannot repair the target's missing method qualification."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "correct-conditional-conservation",
      "evidence": "D009/D039 implement chronological composition; hcover includes every direction; D007/D037 preserve the source's flux orientation; D014/D036 normalize integrals by measured volume.",
      "impact": "The target faithfully represents substantial conservative execution content under Q10, and its auxiliary error estimate is coherent without asserting universal convergence or effectiveness."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The disagreement is resolved by distinguishing the validity of the exact conditional theorem from coverage of the source's intended methods. Its conditional identities follow from the supplied premises, so the reverse implication does not require an unproved claim that all source methods provide those premises. Conversely, conservative sequential execution does not recover the missing constituent-method qualification, and endpoint-only reference conservation does not establish a solved directional problem. The supplied nonconstant witnesses establish satisfiability but not semantic equivalence. The consistent result is therefore not-faithful-weaker, with acceptance withheld and the original source ambiguities preserved."
}
